WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.749
What you’ll carry into the next lesson.

2
00:00:02.029 --> 00:00:05.912
The model call lives on your server, behind your own policy checks.

3
00:00:06.192 --> 00:00:20.976
Synchronous calls fit short work with a machine consumer; streaming fits a person watching; background jobs fit long work, with idempotent side effects because jobs can run twice; batch fits work that can wait, keyed by custom_id.

4
00:00:21.256 --> 00:00:32.243
Every one of these patterns has a failure mode where the provider returns an error, times out, or declines, and in a stream that can happen after you’ve already shown the user half an answer.

5
00:00:32.523 --> 00:00:35.637
Lesson 2 is about handling all of those on purpose.
